<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diodotus I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Diodotus I Soter</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diodotus I was the Seleucid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> who broke away from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in the mid-3rd century BCE and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-bactrian-kingdom">Greco-Bactrian Kingdom</a>. His coins show him first striking in the name of the Seleucid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-ii-theos">Antiochus II</a> with his own portrait, then as king in his own right. He was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diodotus-ii">Diodotus II</a>, and the dynasty was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euthydemus-i">Euthydemus I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diodotus-i.jpg" alt="Diodotus I" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diodotus_I_of_Bactria_wearing_the_diadem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
